# Optional: raises GitHub's public API rate limit for public repositories.
# To create a fine-grained personal access token:
# 1. Open https://github.com/settings/personal-access-tokens and select
#    "Generate new token". Sign in to your GitHub account if prompted.
# 2. Enter a token name, choose an expiration, and select your account as
#    the resource owner.
# 3. Under Repository access, choose "Public Repositories (read-only)".
#    Metadata is read-only by default; no additional permissions are needed
#    to list public repositories for the configured GitHub usernames.
# 4. Generate the token and copy it. Copy this file to .env and paste the
#    token after GITHUB_TOKEN= in .env, not in this example file.
# For Vercel, add GITHUB_TOKEN as a server environment variable. For
# Cloudflare, use `npx wrangler secret put GITHUB_TOKEN` (or .dev.vars
# for local Worker development). Keep the token private and never commit it.
# Token guide: https://docs.github.com/en/authentication/keeping-your-account-and-data-secure/managing-your-personal-access-tokens
GITHUB_TOKEN=
# Set to your final HTTPS domain for canonical URLs and sitemap.
SITE_URL=https://your-domain.example
# node (default), vercel, or cloudflare
DEPLOY_TARGET=node
